1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,925
If your well squeaks, it is a dinner bell.

2
00:00:03,525 --> 00:00:08,112
The Well. Part three of three. The handle.

3
00:00:08,712 --> 00:00:11,711
Your boiled water tastes like a dead man's tooth.

4
00:00:12,852 --> 00:00:14,245
Taste is cheaper than a funeral.

5
00:00:15,732 --> 00:00:20,358
Move the latrine. Seal the lid. Flush the well.

6
00:00:20,958 --> 00:00:25,124
Thirty meters. I dug the first one. I will dig the second.

7
00:00:25,724 --> 00:00:29,345
Wrap the handle. Grease the pivot. Pump slowly.

8
00:00:30,224 --> 00:00:31,644
Three times the well.

9
00:00:33,824 --> 00:00:36,968
Seventy years of killing chickens. Quietly.

10
00:00:37,784 --> 00:00:39,480
At dawn, the strip.

11
00:00:41,024 --> 00:00:42,727
Panic kills faster than thirst.

12
00:00:43,027 --> 00:00:44,208
So does a latrine.

13
00:00:45,704 --> 00:00:49,208
Forty-one people. Zero sick. Four liters each.

14
00:00:49,844 --> 00:00:53,679
The well is clean. It has not rained in fourteen days.

15
00:00:54,704 --> 00:01:00,917
The Well. Part three of three. Follow for the next series.
